{"schema":"ahi.osdr.labpanel.v1","record":{"id":"osdr-osd-575-cmp","source_name":"NASA Open Science Data Repository (OSDR)","source_url":"https://osdr.nasa.gov/bio/repo/data/studies/OSD-575","dataset_accession":"OSD-575","dataset_version":"OSDR metadata version 3","title":"SpaceX Inspiration4 Blood Serum Metabolic Panel and Immune/Cardiac Cytokine Arrays (Comprehensive Metabolic Panel and Multiplex)","downloaded_at":"2026-11-14T11:37:06.986Z","license":null,"access_classification":"Public, open access (downloaded without authentication). Processed tabular data.","file_name":"LSDS-8_Comprehensive_Metabolic_Panel_CMP.upload_SUBMITTED.csv","sha256":"dab247eb794edab59aaaa683c85fd1f2dbf4ae3684872739338e10ead4192a0c","parser_version":"ahi-osdr-import 1.0.0","study_population":"4 crew members (C001, C002, C003, C004): 2 female, 2 male per sample metadata. Study description: \"four private astronauts\". Age: not stated.","mission":"SpaceX Inspiration4 (09/16/2021 to 09/18/2021)","study_design":"Repeated measures on the same 4 subjects at 7 ground time points. Study factors: Time, Spaceflight. Design descriptor: low Earth orbit.","collection_phase":"Pre-flight (L-92, L-44, L-3) and post-flight (R+1, R+45, R+82, R+194). No in-flight samples in this file.","notes":"Comprehensive metabolic panel (CMP) from Serum (serum separator tube). L-n = n days before launch, R+n = n days after return (as labeled in the source). Reference ranges are the lab ranges reported in the source file, not NASA limits. License: not stated in the study metadata.","data_origin":"REAL_PUBLIC"},"study":{"accession":"OSD-575","title":"SpaceX Inspiration4 Blood Serum Metabolic Panel and Immune/Cardiac Cytokine Arrays (Comprehensive Metabolic Panel and Multiplex)","description":"The SpaceX Inspiration4 mission was a 3-day mission with four private astronauts to low Earth orbit that occurred in September 2021. The crew collected biospecimen samples before, during, and after flight. One of these biospecimen collections included whole blood collected via venipuncture, with serum extracted from blood using a serum separator tube (SST). Samples were collected pre-flight (L-92, L-44, L-3) and post-flight (R+1, R+45, R+82). Serum samples were submitted for immune and cardiovascular cytokine biomarker profiling panels at two different companies (Eve Technologies and Alamar), and to Quest Diagnostics for comprehensive metabolic panel testing. Data was used to measure changes in cytokines and metabolic measures during spaceflight. This study derives results from the Comprehensive Metabolic Panel and Multiplex assays, and the blood serum data in this study are related to other studies using data from the same experiment; OSD-569 (whole blood), OSD-570 (peripheral blood mononuclear cells), OSD-571 (plasma), OSD-572 (skin, oral, and nasal swabs), OSD-573 (Dragon capsule samples), OSD-574 (skin biopsy), OSD-656 (urine), and OSD-630 (stool).","release_date":"14-May-2024","mission":{"name":"SpaceX Inspiration4","start":"09/16/2021","end":"09/18/2021"},"publications":[{"title":"The Space Omics and Medical Atlas (SOMA) and international astronaut biobank","doi":"10.1038/s41586-024-07639-y"},{"title":"Collection of Biospecimens from the Inspiration4 Mission Establishes the Standards for the Space Omics and Medical Atlas (SOMA)","doi":"10.1038/s41467-024-48806-z"},{"title":"CAMbank: SST Field Processing v1","doi":"10.17504/protocols.io.81wgbxxo1lpk/v1"}],"related_accessions":["OSD-569","OSD-570","OSD-571","OSD-572","OSD-573","OSD-574","OSD-656","OSD-630"],"study_url":"https://osdr.nasa.gov/bio/repo/data/studies/OSD-575","meta_api_url":"https://osdr.nasa.gov/osdr/data/osd/meta/575"},"file":{"file_name":"LSDS-8_Comprehensive_Metabolic_Panel_CMP.upload_SUBMITTED.csv","url":"https://osdr.nasa.gov/geode-py/ws/studies/OSD-575/download?source=datamanager&file=LSDS-8_Comprehensive_Metabolic_Panel_CMP.upload_SUBMITTED.csv","size_bytes":25275,"sha256":"dab247eb794edab59aaaa683c85fd1f2dbf4ae3684872